// Pseudo-adaptive sampling policy (high level)
function shouldSample(span) {
  // Sample aggressively for high-latency paths
  // Apply per-operation rate caps
  // Allow collector-tail decisions when budget tight
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the impact on SLI accuracy during rollout?
- What metrics would you monitor to trigger automatic rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests planning of safe, multi-region rollout with feature flags and clear rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Progressive rollout
- Feature flags
- Telemetry and SLO-aligned signals
- Cache invalidation/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for rollout gating
const enabled = getFlag("new_api_behavior");
if (enabled && regions.includes(currentRegion)) {
  useNewBehavior();
} else {
  useOldBehavior();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this if some regions have mandatory latency budgets?
- How would you integrate with an incident response playbook?
